---
title: Publishing
---

Discovery is just a static `registry.json` — an array of catalogue entries. There
are three ways to get a plugin to users.

## 1. Community registry

Fork [`logit-plugin-registry`](https://github.com/Martin-Melody/logit-plugin-registry),
add your plugin, open a PR.

```
registry.json                    array of entries
plugins/<plugin-id>/
  manifest.json
  bundle.js                      (or exercises.json for packs)
```

`manifestUrl` and `distribution.bundleUrl` are **repo-relative paths**
(`plugins/<id>/...`), not URLs.

Run the linter before opening the PR — CI runs the same check:

```bash
npm install && npm run lint
```

It validates every entry and manifest, verifies integrity hashes, parses packs,
and loads every code bundle in a real sandbox to confirm it exposes the method
its family needs. First submissions get a human review; version bumps after that
are lighter.

## 2. Your own registry

Host a `registry.json` anywhere static. Users add its URL in
**Plugins → Browse → Sources**. A self-hosted LogIt instance can point its
default there. Entry shape:

```json
{
  "id": "com.you.my-plugin",
  "name": "My Plugin",
  "description": "One sentence.",
  "family": "progression-algorithm",
  "author": "You",
  "manifestUrl": "https://you.example/plugins/my-plugin/manifest.json",
  "tags": ["progression"]
}
```

## 3. No registry

Send someone the manifest URL, the `.logit-pack.json` file, or the raw JSON.
**Plugins → Add** accepts all three.

## Updating

Bump `version` in the manifest, regenerate the `integrity` hash, submit again.
Users get a reviewable "update available" prompt.
